><span><span> West Coast Pilsner</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/14182a28-f5e4-379e-79eb-00424424019f.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🤷‍♀️ Midwest is best: O’fest Edition<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>3 Floyds Munsterfest </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Oktoberfest Marzen<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Great Lakes Oktoberfest</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Great Lakes Biergarten Party Pack</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> with Oktoberfest, German Pils &amp; Apple Pie Eliot Ness</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/5a10770c-a91e-d4d4-527e-c20371a48ee6.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><img src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1f3a2/72.png\" alt=\"🎢\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"> Goodies from </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Fair State</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Pahlay</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Tropical Pale Ale with Citra &amp; Simcoe<br>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Festbier</span></span></span></strong></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/aaee4fad-8eac-0a79-adb5-462edc36b8ba.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span> <img src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/2728/72.png\" alt=\"✨\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"> Freshies from </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Afterglow</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Glowing Places </span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>Hazy IPA with Citra &amp; Superdelic (</span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Aslin</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> collab)<br>•</span></span></span><strong><span><span><span> Bohemian Glow</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Foeder-Aged Czech Amber Lager</span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/5e9d71b1-8939-0ff4-7032-872fc756ec55.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🥨 Grab a pretzel!<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Virginia Beer Co Prost</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> German-style Altbier<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Abomination Drankenstein</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Imperial Marzen<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Victory Festbier</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Aslin Festbier</span></span></span></span></strong></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/5247f935-1d8a-9ff4-f47a-fe980625c1b3.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🐈‍⬛ Seasonal cats on the loose with </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Fat Orange Cat</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Cautionary Tail </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Pumpkin Ale<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Pumpkin Patch Kittens</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> NE IPA with Pumpkin, Spices &amp; Vanilla<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Pumpkin Chai Latte</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Oatmeal Stout</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/01cb09e7-9566-86b8-0a0c-bd508a29139f.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>👻 The horror, pumpkin creep is here!<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Evil Twin Our Most Popular Pumpkin Ale</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Harpoon UFO Pumpkin</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Schlafly Pumpkin</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Shipyard Pumpkinhead</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Hardywood Farmhouse Pumpkin</span></span></span></span></strong></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/94011df8-ac57-3bd0-6820-90a082449c90.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🍎 Fall-foward ciders!<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Downeast Cider Donut</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Wyndridge Imperial Pumpkin</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Wyndridge Caramel Apple</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Lost Boy Pumpkinhead</span></span></span></span></strong></p>\n<p>Melvin Method Krush West Coast IPA</p>\n<p>Final Gravity Mission Control Hazy IPA</p>\n<p>Alternate Ending General Order No 3 Hazy IPA</p>\n<p>Aslin Green Grass West Coast IPA </p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/78dec5a6-f170-a065-c355-70d1d6d2bf76.jpeg\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><strong><span>Mary Taylor Vouvray Estelle Bidault: </span></strong><span><span><span><span>In Estelle Bidault, distributor Mary Taylor has found the perfect collaborator. Estelle is part of a new generation of women reshaping the Loire, choosing to focus entirely on dry Chenin Blanc. We know Chenin Blanc is one of the most underrated grapes on the planet and, well, we were simply blown away by Estelle's version which is grown on Silex soil. Precise with chalky, flinty minerality paired with lemon curd, honey suckle and white flowers. Sustainable.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span>Orealios Robola</span></strong><span>: </span><span><span><span><span>Hailing from mountainous Kefalonia — the largest of the Ionian Islands in western Greece — Orealios is made with Robola, often described as Greece's second noblest white grape behind Assyrtiko. Fun fact, Robola was for years mistakenly believed to be the same as Italy's Ribolla Gialla until modern DNA analysis thwarted that belief. As a wine described by Julie with a series of positive expletives, you might just say we're into this light and bright, coastal-inspired white with grapefruit, lemon and a touch of texture from lees aging. Organic &amp; Hand Harvested.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span>Milou Rose: </span></strong><span><span><span><span>Named after Tintin's beloved little white dog — because who wouldn't want a wine named after the most loyal sidekick in comic book history — Milou is an effortless, crowd-pleasing Rose. Pale and delicate with wild strawberries, fresh cut watermelon, seaside salinity and a clean finish. Organic &amp; Sustainable.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span>Mas Champart Pays d'Herault Rouge</span></strong><span>: </span><span><span><span><span>Decades ago, as an experiment, Matthieu and Isabelle planted a bit of Cabernet Franc in their Saint-Chinian vineyard. This slightly rebellious wine (Saint-Chinian only permits Syrah, Grenache and Mourvèdre) caught the attention of legendary importer Kermit Lynch... and, well, the rest is history. We are equally obsessed with this fresh take on Cab Franc. Terroir-driven with herbs, earthy spice and olive tapenade paired with macerated plums and crunchy berries.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/3a3a67ea-2e23-fba1-6293-58517e8f6f2b.jpeg\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><span><span><span>About once a week we hear a snicker from someone reading the sign in our \"Skin Contact\" section of our wine wall. Promise, we’re here for all the jokes. We made the daring signage switch from “Rose” to “Skin Contact” years ago when Orange wine first splashed onto the scene. The latest Skin <span>*giggle* Contact bottle to hit our shelves: </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Colutta Pinot Grigio Ramato</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>. <br></span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>When you hear Pinot Grigio these days, you likely imagine the pale, crisp, stainless steel Pinot Grigio that has become the world's most ordered house white. It's also the wine that got me into wine! <span>But the original Friulian style of Pinot Grigio was always Ramato — a skin contact wine with a copper color, texture and complexity. </span></span></span></span><span><span><span><span>While orange wine can be made from any white grape, Ramato is specifically and only made with Pinot Grigio. </span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>If you're new to Ramato, Colutta is a great place to start. </span></span></span><span><span><span>When the Pinot Grigio grapes are crushed, the skins </span>— which are actually more of a grayish-pink — spend time with the juice adding not just the coppery color, but a lovely texture, structural complexity and tannins to the wine. The result is </span></span><span><span><span>fresh and bright with notes of peach, apple, and citrus rind plus balanced acidity and gentle, dusty tannins. And because of the added texture and tannins, Colutta is tremendously food friendly, so serve up a pile of prosciutto, order Asian take out, or fire up the grill for salmon. </span></span></span></p>\n<p><em><span><span><span><span>This week’s writeup is brought to you by Beth</span></span></span></span></em></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/c74c8ccc-1842-8f19-1ea4-35e3d6b44646.png\" width=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><span><span><span><span>The </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>FREE local contest </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>for the </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>DC State Fair</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> returns! This is a non-BJCP event and truly one of the most fun contests you’ll enter all year. Make something the committee finds tasty and win! There are categories for both Beer and Cider and there's still time to brew and get your entries in by August 21st. Open to all residents of DC and surrounding counties.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<a href=\"https://us.list-manage.com/1853O0jEyUn?e=01c6cdb4b7&amp;c2id=78b36ba273cb71acbb53a8fce08ea4f0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ENTER DC STATE FAIR BEER CONTEST HERE </a>\n<a href=\"https://us.list-manage.com/DXIlWcJDWdB?e=01c6cdb4b7&amp;c2id=78b36ba273cb71acbb53a8fce08ea4f0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ENTER DC STATE FAIR CIDER CONTEST HERE </a>\n<p>Thanks for your business! See you soon, Beth, Julie &amp; Aidan and the entire Brew Crew</p>",
